-          "claim": "For $n\\ge1$, let $p_n(t)=\\sum_{k=0}^na_kT_k(t)$. By [F1]–[F3] and [F10], $Q_{n,[a,b]}(f)=d\\sum_k a_k\\int_{-1}^1T_k(t)\\,dt=d\\int_{-1}^1p_n(t)\\,dt$. The affine substitution [F9] makes this $\\int_a^bP(x)\\,dx$ for $P(x)=p_n((x-m)/d)$, and [F2] identifies $P$ with the interpolant pullback. For $n=0$, [F1] is the integral of the constant polynomial $P(x)=f(m)$ by [F9]. Thus $Q_{n,[a,b]}(f)=\\int_a^bP(x)\\,dx$ in every case.",
