           "source": "def-na-clenshaw-curtis-quadrature",
           "source_section": "Definition",
-          "quote": "Let $a<b$, $m=(a+b)/2$, $d=(b-a)/2$, and $f\\in C[a,b]$. For $n\\ge1$, set $g(t):=f(m+dt)$ on $[-1,1]$, let $y_j=g(\\cos(j\\pi/n))$, and form $a_0,\\ldots,a_n$ from the DCT-I coefficients in [[thm-na-clenshaw-curtis-interpolation-coefficients]]. With the Chebyshev moments $\\mu_k$ of [[lem-na-chebyshev-integral-moments]], define\n$$Q_{n,[a,b]}(f):=d\\sum_{k=0}^{n}a_k\\mu_k.$$\nFor $n=0$, define instead\n$$Q_{0,[a,b]}(f):=(b-a)f(m),$$\nthe midpoint rule. This is the explicit endpoint and zero-degree convention for Clenshaw–Curtis quadrature. The sums and coefficients are exact real quantities; finite-precision evaluation is a separate algorithm.",
+          "quote": "Let $a<b$, $m=(a+b)/2$, $d=(b-a)/2$, and $f\\in C[a,b]$. For $n\\ge1$, set $g(t):=f(m+dt)$ on $[-1,1]$, let $y_j=g(\\cos(j\\pi/n))$, and form $a_0,\\ldots,a_n$ from the DCT-I coefficients in [[thm-na-clenshaw-curtis-interpolation-coefficients]]. With the Chebyshev moments $\\mu_k$ of [[lem-na-chebyshev-integral-moments]], define\n$$Q_{n,[a,b]}(f):=d\\sum_{k=0}^{n}a_k\\mu_k.$$\nFor $n=0$, define instead\n$$Q_{0,[a,b]}(f):=(b-a)f(m),$$\nthe midpoint rule. This is the explicit endpoint and zero-degree convention for Clenshaw\u2013Curtis quadrature. The sums and coefficients are exact real quantities; finite-precision evaluation is a separate algorithm.",
